WHY THIS LICENCE

The NonCommercial condition is the author's deliberate choice, applied
consistently across the scripts he maintains with Caelo Works. Unlike some of
those scripts, it is not imposed here by any upstream work: the one third-party
component this script derives from is permissive.

That component is the astrometric grid computation in
mosaictoolbox/MT_Astrometry.js, derived from the MosaicByCoordinates script and
used under the PixInsight Class Library License 2.0. That licence allows
commercial use and does not require NonCommercial terms; the NonCommercial
condition above is added by the author over his own work, which the permissive
upstream licence allows. What the upstream licence does require — that its
copyright notice, its list of conditions, its restrictions and its disclaimer
travel with every copy, together with the PixInsight acknowledgment — is
recorded in full in NOTICE.md.

NOTICE.md is part of the licence terms, not documentation. Redistribute it with
the work. The other works this script builds on are attributed there too.

